@startuml acp-turn
!include theme.iuml
title Crafty — Codex through ACP, with durable application state
autonumber
actor User
participant "Browser" as UI
participant "API / durable state" as API
participant "ACP supervisor" as Relay
participant "Codex ACP adapter\n+ App Server" as Agent
participant "Crafty MCP" as MCP
participant "CAD launcher" as CAD

Relay -> Agent : initialize(protocolVersion=1, capabilities)
Agent --> Relay : chosen version + image / MCP / resume capabilities
note over Relay, Agent
  Register the reader and request handlers before session setup.
  Drain stderr separately. Authentication uses private agent state.
end note
Relay -> Agent : session/new(cwd, mcpServers)
Agent --> Relay : sessionId
Relay -> API : bind chatId to sessionId + runtimeEpoch

User -> UI : capture several views; annotate selected images
UI -> API : upload bytes; finalize assets
API --> UI : ready asset IDs + source relationships
UI -> API : submit message(clientMessageId, assetIds, replyTo)
API -> API : atomically save message + turn + dispatch command
API --> UI : accepted message + event cursor
API -> Relay : dispatch once; hold per-chat turn ownership
Relay -> Agent : session/prompt(text + asset references)
Agent -> MCP : asset_fetch(assetId)
MCP -> API : fetch scoped asset bytes
API --> MCP : verified MIME + bytes + digest
MCP -> MCP : write into agent-visible chat folder
MCP --> Agent : assetId + localPath
Agent -> Agent : open local image with image-view tool
note over Relay, Agent
  Keep this request open through the entire v1 turn.
  Continue reading updates AND agent requests concurrently.
  Files are the baseline image handoff; opening them provides vision input.
  ACP inline image blocks are an optional alternative.
end note

loop text / tool activity during the turn
  Agent -> Relay : session/update(message chunk or tool patch)
  Relay -> API : event(epoch, localSeq, raw frame)
  API -> API : persist projection + durable event sequence
  API --> UI : event(seq, chatId, turnId, operationId?)
end

opt the agent requests measurements or photos
  Agent -> MCP : request_input(schema, imageAssetIds)
  MCP -> API : create durable interaction
  API --> MCP : interactionId + typed card data
  MCP --> Agent : structured result + text fallback
  API --> UI : interaction.created
  note over UI, Agent
    Tool returns promptly. The agent can end its turn.
    Form or capture submission becomes a later user message.
    Native ACP elicitation is a separately negotiated capability.
  end note
end

opt the agent generates a sketch
  Agent -> Agent : image generation -> local output file
  Agent -> MCP : asset_publish(localPath, kind, sourceAssetIds)
  MCP -> API : ingest completed bytes; create immutable asset
  API --> MCP : assetId + typed card reference
  MCP --> Agent : persisted asset reference
  API --> UI : asset.published
end

opt the agent generates a part
  Agent -> MCP : cad_build(sourcePath, inputs)
  MCP -> API : upload frozen source; create job with active turn scope
  API --> MCP : jobId + operationId
  MCP --> Agent : durable job reference
  CAD -> API : lease job(attemptId)
  CAD -> CAD : isolated FreeCAD build
  CAD -> API : stage STEP output; complete build attempt
  Agent -> MCP : cad_status(jobId) / bounded cad_wait(jobId)
  MCP -> API : read build state; fetch completed outputs
  API --> MCP : staged output bytes
  MCP -> MCP : materialize STEP in agent-visible folder
  MCP --> Agent : stepPath + sourcePath + jobId
  Agent -> MCP : model_publish(stepPath, sourcePath, parentRevisionId)
  MCP -> API : ingest exact local files; create publication operation
  API --> MCP : operationId + processing card reference
  MCP --> Agent : durable publication reference
  CAD -> API : lease verification job
  CAD -> CAD : reopen submitted STEP -> validate -> GLB + PNG
  CAD -> API : upload derivatives; complete(attemptId)
  API -> API : check lease + cancellation fence; publish revision atomically
  API --> UI : revision.ready(asset manifest)
  note over Agent, CAD
    model_publish also accepts an already available local STEP + source.
    Build completion and model publication have separate job states.
    Agent can fetch the published verification PNG for visual review.
  end note
end

alt ordinary completion
  Agent --> Relay : original session/prompt response(stopReason)
  Relay -> API : finish turn; release prompt slot
else user presses Stop
  UI -> API : cancel active turn
  API -> API : revoke job publication for this turn
  API -> Relay : cancel turn command
  Relay -> Agent : session/cancel notification (no response expected)
  API -> CAD : cancel linked foreground jobs
  CAD -> CAD : stop attempt containers; discard unpublished outputs
  Agent -> Relay : final updates may still arrive
  Agent --> Relay : original session/prompt response(cancelled)
  Relay -> API : mark turn cancelled; release prompt slot
  note over API, Agent
    Pending permission requests resolve as cancelled.
    A deadline without acknowledgement fences the old runtime.
    Late frames remain diagnostics; they cannot publish a revision.
  end note
end

UI -> API : reconnect(after durable event sequence)
API --> UI : replay application events or snapshot + cursor
note over UI, Relay
  Browser reconnect does not create or reload an ACP session.
  Only runtime recovery uses negotiated session/resume or session/load.
end note
@enduml
